#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# r_stability_conditions

#% text
# `r_stability_conditions(eqs, vs, n)` gives, for each equilibrium of the autonomous recurrence equations eqs in the unknown sequences vs, a pair `[point, condition]`: the condition under which the equilibrium is asymptotically stable.

#% text
# `r_stability_conditions(eqs, vs, n, points)` considers the given points.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The recurrences are written as a first-order system; at each fixed point (from `r_fixed_points`) the condition is that every eigenvalue of the Jacobian has absolute value below 1. Numbers decide it.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
r_stability_conditions(a(n + 1) == (1/2)*a(n), a(n), n)
#% output
#= [[[0], true]]

#% cell
r_stability_conditions(y(n + 1) == a*y(n), y, n)
#% output
#= [[[0], -1 < a and a < 1]]

#% cell
r_stability_conditions(a(n + 1) == 2*(1 - a(n))*a(n), a(n), n)
#% output
#= [[[0], false], [[1/2], true]]

#% cell
r_stability_conditions([y(n + 1) == 3 - z(n), z(n + 1) == (1 - y(n))/2], [y(n), z(n)], n)
#% output
#= [[[5, -2], true]]

#% cell
r_stability_conditions(a(n + 2) == a(n + 1)*a(n)^2, a(n), n)
#% output
#= [[[-1, -1], false], [[0, 0], true], [[1, 1], false]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
